{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421326-2e-mortal-antagonists","id":1421326,"title":"[2E] Mortal Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-01T12:38:06-08:00","id":1421326,"title":"[2E] Mortal Antagonists","content":"I'm starting Origin tier game - and want to confront my players with some mortal enemies - like russian mob or esoterics archeologiests. I look for stats of those for Scion - or will make them if those are none existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T13:38:20-08:00","id":1421332,"title":"","content":"On Origin page 144-145 you have antagonist archetypes. The Mook, Professional, VIllain and Monster. Just use them as references and flesh them out a little if you need to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T15:53:23-08:00","id":1421354,"title":"","content":"To build on that... Remember, your antagonists are as deadly as you need them to be. If you need a mortal antagonist to be Sid the Squid, the absolute D-tier mook, then you can stat him that way.<br /> <br /> If you need a mortal antagonist to be goddamn John Wick and so tenacious and deadly that even Heroes know better than to take him lightly, you can give him the Villain archetype and some custom Flairs and Qualities to make him a legitimate threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T07:33:47-08:00","id":1421441,"title":"","content":"<b>Notice</b>: I will edit each new Archetypes below when ending it\u2019s write-up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Mafia/Mob</b></span><br /> <br /> I propose here typical Mafia hierarchy, based on this Italian kind \u2013 however most crime syndicates follow very similar structures. As Storyguide, add some cultural and local variants to possible traits those Archetypes have. Here is typical syndicate \u2013 called <i>Family</i> \u2013 structure:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mafia_family_structure_tree.en.svg/1024px-Mafia_family_structure_tree.en.svg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mafia_family_structure_tree.en.svg/1024px-Mafia_family_structure_tree.en.svg.png \" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MOOK \u2013 Mob \u2018Soldier\u2019</b></span><br /> <br /> Soldiers are lowers ranked members of each Mafia. They are typical doing \u2018convincing\u2019 for smaller targets of Family - intimidation and extortion. They are also foot soldiers in times of gang wars between syndicates.<br /> <br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Mook<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Group Tactics, Twitchy<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Dread Gaze ( Intimidation ). Spray n\u2019 Pray (H&amp;K submachine gun)<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To fulfill command of Copo or Don<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Intimidation, Combat, Shooting<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4</b>): Athletics, Streetwise<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 2<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>H&amp;K submachine gun</b> \u2013 Enhancement 2, Ballistic, Ranged: Medium, Automatic, Quality 1<br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 ( Close Combat Training )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>PROFESSIONAL \u2013 Capo(regime)</b></span><br /> <br /> Also known simply as Captain, it\u2019s rank is marking him as veteran of Family operations. Is leader for each crew of Soldiers and has major social status and influence in the organization. He answers directly to Don ( Boss ) or an Underboss.<br /> <b>\u2018Capo has strength in his crew</b> \u2013 in brackets are his stats when surrounded by his crew. He also rising his crews Defense, Enhancement and Health by 1.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Professional<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>A Cut Above (+1 Enhancement, Choose from: Combat/Intimidation/Shooting ), Group Tactics, Institutional Disbelief, Twitchy, Slothful Resilience ( Mob dedication )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Dread Gaze ( Intimidation ). Spray n\u2019 Pray (H&amp;K submachine gun), Long Arm ( Boxing grip ), Inspiration ( Families Command ), Seeing Red<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To fulfill command of Don<br /> <b>Primary Pool (7):</b> Combat, Intimidation, Leadership, Shooting<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (5</b><b>):</b> Athletics, Streetwise<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 3<br /> <b>Health: </b>2 (\u20183)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 (\u20184)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5 (+2e )<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>H&amp;K submachine gun</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), Ballistic, Ranged: Medium, Automatic, Quality 1<br /> <b>Pistol ( Desert Eagle ) </b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Loud (-1), Piercing (2), Ranged (0)<br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), ( Close Combat Training )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>VILLAIN \u2013 Assassin</b><br /> <br /> <b>VILLAIN \u2013 Don ( Boss )</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-17-2020, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T09:38:01-08:00","id":1424558,"title":"","content":"First take on the Capo as Professional Archetype for Mob...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>PROFESSIONAL \u2013 Capo(regime)</b></span><br /> <br /> Also known simply as Captain, it\u2019s rank is marking him as veteran of Family operations. Is leader for each crew of Soldiers and has major social status and influence in the organization. He answers directly to Don ( Boss ) or an Underboss.<br /> <b>\u2018Capo has strength in his crew</b> \u2013 in brackets are his stats when surrounded by his crew. He also rising his crews Defense, Enhancement and Health by 1.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Professional<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>A Cut Above (+1 Enhancement, Choose from: Combat/Intimidation/Shooting ), Group Tactics, Institutional Disbelief, Twitchy, Slothful Resilience ( Mob dedication )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Dread Gaze ( Intimidation ). Spray n\u2019 Pray (H&amp;K submachine gun), Long Arm ( Boxing grip ), Inspiration ( Families Command ), Seeing Red<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To fulfill command of Don<br /> <b>Primary Pool (7):</b> Combat, Intimidation, Leadership, Shooting<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (5</b><b>):</b> Athletics, Streetwise<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 3<br /> <b>Health: </b>2 (\u20183)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3 (\u20184)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5 (+2e )<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>H&amp;K submachine gun</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), Ballistic, Ranged: Medium, Automatic, Quality 1<br /> <b>Pistol ( Desert Eagle ) </b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Loud (-1), Piercing (2), Ranged (0)<br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 (\u20182), ( Close Combat Training )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-17-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T11:06:15-08:00","id":1424576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421326-2e-mortal-antagonists?p=1421354#post1421354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To build on that... Remember, your antagonists are as deadly as you need them to be. If you need a mortal antagonist to be Sid the Squid, the absolute D-tier mook, then you can stat him that way.<br /> <br /> If you need a mortal antagonist to be goddamn John Wick and so tenacious and deadly that even Heroes know better than to take him lightly, you can give him the Villain archetype and some custom Flairs and Qualities to make him a legitimate threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>S&amp;M will likely expand on the diegetic setting niche of Saints as \u201cMortals who punch above their weight class\u201d. Not disagreeing on the use of qualities and flairs for mortal antagonists, I just know some people get hung up on setting verisimilitude and may feel they need more justification for a mortal being able to hold their own with a Scion, and I think Saints are going to help fill in that niche.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also played at my own table with Fatebound mortal npcs picking up qualities and flairs that fit their role (including as nemeses) as the tides of fate backs them up in that specific capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T19:45:12-08:00","id":1424642,"title":"","content":"General schema of <b>Loyalists of Thule </b>as Antagonists group. I will edit the post when preparing stats for those archetypes.<br /> <br /> <b>Notice</b>: This is antagonistic version of <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> group, adapted as Antagonists for the <b>Scion</b> games. For more information on Loyalists, see <b>HtV</b> corebook 1st or 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Esoterica Hunters \u2013 Loyalists of Thule</b></span> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/01NDCSLLKwzbOgx7erIjQXPsMpycIKuqfVFTISVuvl7CXfSBVSLldxsXthqTZ1AZpV2UH-qnqM0xyj0JZgk093FFrYaxe-pz0xL5D-pIgqhPnRFLzT-TK7YXpQG_\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <b>Thule Gehellschaft</b> (Thule Society) was German occult group that started in 1918, revolving around research into nations mystical origins \u2013 and to uncover all the secrets of the World. It quickly evolved, taking more and more political ideas into it, springing into German National Socialist party, a.k.a. the Nazis. Thule still existed, but only as esoteric arm of the party \u2013 until it was officially banned with other lodges and societies in 1937. Unofficially, Thule members still worked, sometimes for Nazis in World War 2, sometimes on their own hand. After War, Thule separated it clearly from day-to-day politics, going totally underground, double down on it\u2019s esoteric goals, starting their chapter houses where they can. Today, Loyalists are renown artifacts hunters and occult scientist \u2013 they only have problem with sticking with bad people to get to their researches.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MOOK \u2013 Thule Researcher</b></span><br /> <br /> Singular researcher, expert on some &lt;Occult topic&gt; \u2013 and getting it.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Mook<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To uncover secrets of &lt;Occult topic&gt;<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Cross-Training, Helpless Fascination ( &lt;Occult topic&gt; )<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Occult, Academics<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4): </b>Shooting, Persuasion<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 2<br /> <b>Health: </b>1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 ( Close Combat Training )<br /> <b>Pistol</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Piercing (2), Ranged (0), Reset (-1)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MOOK \u2013 \u2018Far-Right\u2019 Muscle</b></span><br /> <br /> Thule is independent from day-to-day politics \u2013 but still likes to employ strength of those that sympathize with \u2018Far-Right\u2019 in nowadays. If they give themselves to be used - why not use them. Most researchers still need good muscle guys to cover their backs.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Mook<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To help \u2018great and in-danger empire\u2019 / white race / etc.<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Stand Tall, Improvised Weapon ( +1 Enhancement for Improvised Weapons, counted below )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Seeing Red, Selfless Shield<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Combat, Intimidation,<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4):</b> Athletics, Streetwise, Politics<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 2<br /> <b>Health: </b>1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Improvised Weapon ( Club, knife, etc. )</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Delicate ( On attack roll with any 1s, weapon is destroyed and need new one be created )<br /> <b>Metal Chain</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Bashing (0), Melee (0), Reach (1)<br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 ( Close Combat Training )<br /> <br /> <b>PROFESSIONAL \u2013 Chapter Leader</b><br /> <br /> Leader of researchers in region, master of experts in some particular occult field \u2013 but, also, good coordinator of others works.<br /> <br /> <b>PROFESSIONAL \u2013 Special Units / like Neo-Nazis Flame Throwers? /</b><br /> <br /> Expert \u2018direct\u2019 units to disarm monsters. Legacy of Nazis experiments groups, many times as Super Soldiers.<br /> <br /> <b>VILLAIN \u2013 Leading Archeologist</b><br /> <br /> Expert of experts in some particular occult field. Living only to uncover knowledge. At all costs!<br /> <br /> <b>MONSTERS \u2013 Many \ud83d\ude09</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-30-2021, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T02:24:01-08:00","id":1424670,"title":"","content":"The Thule Society are a official Vigil so I don't see a problem here. Mind you, I always felt it was weird that they were a heroic group in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T04:47:47-08:00","id":1424684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421326-2e-mortal-antagonists?p=1424670#post1424670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thule Society are a official Vigil so I don't see a problem here. Mind you, I always felt it was weird that they were a heroic group in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are considered a heroic group because their founders used to be active Nazis and now profess to be deeply ashamed of that, so they strive to stop something like Nazi Germany to happen again while hunting for monsters and forbidden lore. Of course, they probably have their own dark secrets too, at the discretion of the game group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T05:26:02-08:00","id":1425915,"title":"","content":"I would steer far away from using Nazi or Nazi-like antagonists in Scion unless they were portrayed as ineffectual and pathetic, for reasons described in the now closed &quot;God and the Alt-Right&quot; thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23975-pxgentleman","name":"PXGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T08:26:58-08:00","id":1426587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23975-pxgentleman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23975\" data-vbnamecard=\"23975\">PXGentleman</a> - Great for your table, those write-ups are for people wanting to use 'dark Thule' in their games.<br /> <br /> \u200bDrafts of <i>Thule Researcher</i> and <i>'Far-Right' Muscle</i> to talk about.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MOOK \u2013 Thule Researcher</b></span><br /> <br /> Singular researcher, expert on some &lt;Occult topic&gt; \u2013 and getting it.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Mook<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To uncover secrets of &lt;Occult topic&gt;<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Cross-Training, Helpless Fascination ( &lt;Occult topic&gt; )<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Occult, Academics<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4): </b>Shooting, Persuasion<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 2<br /> <b>Health: </b>1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 ( Close Combat Training )<br /> <b>Pistol</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Piercing (2), Ranged (0), Reset (-1)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>MOOK \u2013 \u2018Far-Right\u2019 Muscle</b></span><br /> <br /> Thule is independent from day-to-day politics \u2013 but still likes to employ strength of those that sympathize with \u2018Far-Right\u2019 in nowadays. If they give themselves to be used - why not use them. Most researchers still need good muscle guys to cover their backs.<br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Mook<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To help \u2018great and in-danger empire\u2019 / white race / etc.<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Stand Tall, Improvised Weapon ( +1 Enhancement for Improvised Weapons, counted below )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Seeing Red, Selfless Shield<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Combat, Intimidation,<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4):</b> Athletics, Streetwise, Politics<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 2<br /> <b>Health: </b>1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Improvised Weapon ( Club, knife, etc. )</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Delicate ( On attack roll with any 1s, weapon is destroyed and need new one be created )<br /> <b>Metal Chain</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Bashing (0), Melee (0), Reach (1)<br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1 ( Close Combat Training )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T21:34:55-07:00","id":1463054,"title":"","content":"We are almost year later and my <b>Scion</b> game with Thule need a really, heavy punchers on Legend 1 players Scions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So what do you guys think about them?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Scion Hunters</b></span><br /> <br /> Thule Commando variant \u2013 best of the best \u2013 they are given Anti-Scion weapons to make defeating pesky Scions easier. Finding Atlantean tech, Thule reverse engineered some Relics as weapons that nullified Ichor in Scions blood. Only problem is that it needs the Scion\u2019s Ichor in the first place\u2026 Scion Hunters are for fighting those Chosen of Gods \u2013 or to steal their precious Ichor, to create more this Anti-Ichor weapons. Often they are lead by the Scions working for Thule. ( Yes, there are some traitors like those. )<br /> <br /> <b>Archetype:</b> Nemesis ( Hero Archetype )<br /> <b>Drive:</b> To hunt &amp; fight Scions<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Mystical Arsenal ( Hero, Anti-Ichor Rifle), Group Tactics, Heavily Armored ( +1 Hard, + 2 Soft Armor ), Cross-Training<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Spray N\u2019 Pray, Selfless Shield. I Have Friends, Detonation ( Hero, Hand Grenades ), Penetrator ( Hero, pierce Armor ), Suck It Up ( Hero, Health reset &amp; bonus on attack )<br /> <b>Primary Pool (11):</b> Close Combat, Ranged Combat, Intimidation<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (9): </b>Athletics, Occult<br /> <b>Desperation Pool:</b> 6<br /> <b>Health: </b>6 (?*)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6 (?*)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Anti-Ichor Rifle </b>\u2013 Enhancement 2 \u2013 <b>Tags:</b> Firearm (2), Anti-Ichor ( Legend Drain, 5 ), Lethal (0), Loud (-1), Piercing (2), Ranged (0), Two-Handed (-1) / Because of <i>Mystical Arsenal</i>, can be +4 Enhancement with Tension 1 /<br /> <b>Military Knife </b>\u2013 Enhancement 2, Lethal (0), Piercing (2)<br /> <b>Fists in Armor Gloves</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Close Combat Training<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6CLqXNt.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Anti-Ichor ( Legend Drain ) \u2013 Weapon Tag 5</b></span><br /> <br /> This weapon is made to fight with Scions. Made by foul magic or advanced technology, is dedicated in attacking godly Ichor in veins of Scions. Each hit by this weapon spend Legend point in the target. When target is lowered to Legend 0 by this, Scion loose access to Purviews and other magic and Immortal Knacks \u2013 but not Heroic Knacks. Target can still use Relics that do not need the spending of Legend, like Origin Scions can. Regaining Legend lost by hit with weapon requires the close contact with Purviews sources for one hour, at least one for each Legend point. Scion with Sky Purview need to glide in the sky, holder of Fortune Purview need to go to casino, etc.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/KdNuxJO.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:25:12-07:00","id":1464187,"title":"","content":"Liked a lot of what I saw here. The Thule society looks like a cool type of Origin antagonist and that anyone can reskin in many different shapes, with the atention previously mentioned about the complications in portraying that kind of political thinking.<br /> <br /> The Legend Drain mechanics are also good because they seem serious enough to be a worry, but not so drastical as &quot;Drain Level&quot; and the likes are in D&amp;D. Since the Legend &quot;drained&quot; is not transfered to another place, I think &quot;Legend Drain&quot; is more to &quot;Legend Ceasing&quot; (it just interrupts your access to it &quot;for a while&quot;), but just a very small detail. The work is really great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T02:41:48-07:00","id":1481585,"title":"","content":"Got to prepare some new mortal antagonists, this time from Cops and Security.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Cops and Security</b></span><br /> <br /> Archetypes based on Cops Examples ( Sc 2E <b>Origin </b>p. 154 ) Quote from <b>Origin</b> to start.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Beat Cop ( Origin )</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Archetype</b>: Mook<br /> <b>Qualities</b>: None<br /> <b>Drive: To</b> serve and protect<br /> <b>Primary Pool (5):</b> Combat, Investigation, Personal Interactions<br /> <b>Secondary Pool (4):</b> Athletics, Alertness<br /> <b>Desperation Pool: </b>2<br /> <b>Health:</b> 1<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 3<br /> <br /> And here is my new entry for Mortal Antagonists - your typical 'black suit security'.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Security Guard Pro - PROFESSIONAL (Origin)/ FOE (Hero)</b></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/68kw4Li.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Professional, contracted security officer \u2013 called often \u2018suits\u2019, with black sunglasses. Often times, veteran from army or police, now privately contracted.<br /> Stats for Hero level are in brackets []<br /> <br /> <b>Drive:</b> To protect contracted target<br /> <b>Qualities: </b>Group Tactics ( Origin ), Twitchy ( Origin, counted below ), Stand Tall ( Origin ), Cross-Training ( Origin ), Slothful Resilience ( Origin )<br /> <b>Flairs:</b> Selfless Shield ( Origin ), Dread Gaze ( Origin ), Seeing Red ( Origin ), Spray N\u2019 Pray ( Origin )<br /> <b>Primary Pool:</b> 7 ( Close Combat, Firearms )<br /> <b>Secondary Pool:</b> 5 ( Perception, Survival )<br /> <b>Desperation Pool</b>: 3<br /> <b>Health:</b> 2 [1]<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2 [1]<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 5+2e [4+2e]<br /> <b>Extras:</b> A Cut Above (+1 Enhancement on Close Combat and Firearms rolls, beside weapons bonus )<br /> <br /> <b>Attacks:</b><br /> <b>Fists</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Close Combat Training<br /> <b>Pistol</b> \u2013 Enhancement 1, Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Piercing (2), Ranged (0), Reset (-1)<br /> <b>Submachine Gun</b> ( From high end clients ) \u2013 Enhancement 2, Automatic (2), Firearm (0), Lethal (0), Ranged (0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-21-2022, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T15:52:09-07:00","id":1481689,"title":"","content":"There's probably something interesting to be done with a group of anti-Scion/Pantheon mortals who want to steal the power of the gods for themselves. &quot;Prometheans&quot; or &quot;New Gods&quot; or &quot;Rex Mundi&quot; or something along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T16:12:38-07:00","id":1481691,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Sun Wokung seems like a good naming inspiration for a group like that. He had a supernatural birth but was more or less a 'normal' talking monkey who learned martial arts and taoist sorcery before proceeding to plunder a truly epic number of artifacts and techniques from the heavens until he became so OP that the gods had to run crying to a Buddha for help getting him to cut it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T17:30:11-07:00","id":1481699,"title":"","content":"If you could come up with a time traveler, they would be scary opponents for a Scion. Someone like the Doctor could be a threat to a god. A less capable time traveler could be a threat to a Scion. <br /> <br /> A time traveler fanatical enough to reshape history in a massive way could use even a very limited means of time travel in ways that could break gods. They could also help gods in ways that could disrupt whole pantheons. <br /> <br /> Picture an Irish nationalist, a good and kind woman, who finds a time fissure and how to navigate it. She gains a means of writing down in Latin a large number of Celtic myths, including the Celtic creation stories (few cultures have only one). She hides these written records in a sturdy amphora that she has made waterproof, and hides the amphora in a secure cave. Later, after returning to the present, she &quot;finds&quot; the amphora.<br /> <br /> Because the amphora and its contents are from ancient times and are now fully old enough to be from the late Roman period when a scribe might have recorded this information, the records past all tests of authenticity. A major part of whatever fate binding has been done on the Tautha Dedanna has been undone. If any data of the Welsh or Gallic gods has been included, and major blow has been struck against the Theoi which they can't parry. <br /> <br /> Time travelers can be benign, or mainly so, like my example. Others can be toxic. Picture a neo-Nazi who has decided that killing FDR as a child will allow Hitler to win WWII (it wouldn't, but the damage would be incredible). Picture someone trying to be a &quot;White Savior.&quot; They could derail whole cultures while trying to help. As they'd be less predictable than out and out villains, they'd be by far the bigger threat. Watch the old Doctor Who episode &quot;The Aztecs.&quot; Then imagine Barbara as an independent time traveler passionately in love with Aztec art and culture and fiercely determined to &quot;save&quot; then. Courageous, self-righteous, and wrong, picture a more devastating foe. Consider the education a British woman like Barbara Wright would have received in the late 1950s. She could be completely non-racist, but raised in the context of Imperialism, her skewed worldview, combined with her real virtues, would make her an overwhelming opponent for a group of Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-22-2022, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T19:56:33-07:00","id":1481717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421326-2e-mortal-antagonists?p=1481689#post1481689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's probably something interesting to be done with a group of anti-Scion/Pantheon mortals who want to steal the power of the gods for themselves. &amp;quot;Prometheans&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;New Gods&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Rex Mundi&amp;quot; or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, 'Prometheus Unbound'? \ud83d\ude0e It's literally why <b>Aeon</b> book was called that in first place - to point on 'humanity stealing the powers of the gods'. \ud83d\ude0e ( But in <b>Trinity Aeon</b> setting.) / I've just listened to the interview about it. \ud83d\ude09 /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-23-2022, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T20:03:52-07:00","id":1481718,"title":"","content":"I dunno, honestly I personally really don't like Prometheus as the name for a group like that. He wasn't a mortal who stole divine power, he was a divine being who gave humans power without them having to put in any work themselves to obtain it. It just seems like a bad fit for mortals who want to seize power with their own hands instead of being content with the power gods see fit to hand out to humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T00:43:49-07:00","id":1481735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1421326-2e-mortal-antagonists?p=1481718#post1481718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, honestly I personally really don't like Prometheus as the name for a group like that. He wasn't a mortal who stole divine power, he was a divine being who gave humans power without them having to put in any work themselves to obtain it. It just seems like a bad fit for mortals who want to seize power with their own hands instead of being content with the power gods see fit to hand out to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. \ud83e\udd14. The House of Frankenstein? Or is that too cheesy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T11:03:42-07:00","id":1481766,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, naming it after a scientist could work. Like naming it after Tesla for him being the one to 'tame' lightning into something usable by everyone with his AC electricity. Or maybe go with something more warlike and name themselves after the Manhattan project and the creation of nuclear weapons (I would recommend against using one of the scientists involved there because a lot of them like Oppenheimer are ashamed of their work and really would not appreciate it). Or yeah, Frankenstein would be great to since he tried to steal the power of creating new life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-23-2022, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}